"],"issue":"5","journal":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","pages":"901-911","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187175095"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a309aedb-bb1e-46ad-ab2b-0558b59afe58"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"One sixth of Amazonian tree diversity is dependent on river floodplains","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-744990","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Very few forests take up as much space in contemporary Western imagination as the Amazon. It is the archetypical mythological forest that many people want to save and even more people want to exploit. Over the years, it has been the object of multiple campaigns to ‘save the rainforest’ from resource extraction both within South America and beyond, within scientific communities as well as broader publics. This article addresses a concern with how to extract the resources of the Amazon Forest in ways that are more sustainable than past and contemporary logging, mining and farming. This concern is promoted by Brazilian scientists who have allied themselves with well-intended tech industry initiatives and small-scale entrepreneurs. We refer to this combination of conservation with extraction as salvage technoscience, an approach currently dominating the struggle for the resources of the Amazon by attempting to reconcile the opposing views of the forest as an economic asset and as an object to be preserved. Our contribution thus demonstrates the interwoven nature of capitalist extraction and environmental conservation under the auspices of technoscientific progress.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Santos da Costa, Priscila","Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754072"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Amazon Forest","Environmental Conservation","Salvage Technoscience","Sustainable Resource Extraction","Technoscientific Progress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"salvage technoscience conserving and extracting the value of the amazon rainforest","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105843079/Salvage_Technoscience_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754072","ids":["itu-58b977af-421f-4a2f-8a16-08ce0950c4ce"],"keyword":["Amazon Forest","Environmental Conservation","Salvage Technoscience","Sustainable Resource Extraction","Technoscientific Progress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FC50CB4B508150101576AF5FBD47358A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105843079/Salvage_Technoscience_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Priscila","key":"santosdacostapau","last":"Santos da Costa","locid":"9734ef6f-09d1-4ca1-b968-6ad34872d504","name":"Santos da Costa, Priscila","orcid":"0000-0003-2439-9960","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-58b977af-421f-4a2f-8a16-08ce0950c4ce"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Salvage technoscience: Conserving and extracting the value of the Amazon Rainforest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754072","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"microbeMASST, a taxonomically informed mass spectrometry (MS) search tool, tackles limited microbial metabolite annotation in untargeted metabolomics experiments. Leveraging a curated database of >60,000 microbial monocultures, users can search known and unknown MS/MS spectra and link them to their respective microbial producers via MS/MS fragmentation patterns. Identification of microbe-derived metabolites and relative producers without a priori knowledge will vastly enhance the understanding of microorganisms’ role in ecology and human health.","author_count":109,"contributors":["Zuffa, Simone","Schmid, Robin","Bauermeister, Anelize","Paulo, Paulo Wender","Caraballo-Rodriguez, Andres M.","El Abiead, Yasin","Aron, Allegra T.","Gentry, Emily C.","Zemlin, Jasmine","Meehan, Michael J.","Avalon, Nicole E.","Cichewicz, Robert H.","Buzun, Ekaterina","Terrazas, Marvic Carrillo","Hsu, Chia Yun","Oles, Renee","Ayala, Adriana Vasquez","Zhao, Jiaqi","Chu, Hiutung","Kuijpers, Mirte C.M.","Jackrel, Sara L.","Tugizimana, Fidele","Nephali, Lerato Pertunia","Dubery, Ian A.","Madala, Ntakadzeni Edwin","Moreira, Eduarda Antunes","Costa-Lotufo, Leticia Veras","Lopes, Norberto Peporine","Rezende-Teixeira, Paula","Jimenez, Paula C.","Rimal, Bipin","Patterson, Andrew D.","Traxler, Matthew F.","Pessotti, Rita de Cassia","Alvarado-Villalobos, Daniel","Tamayo-Castillo, Giselle","Chaverri, Priscila","Escudero-Leyva, Efrain","Quiros-Guerrero, Luis Manuel","Bory, Alexandre Jean","Joubert, Juliette","Rutz, Adriano","Wolfender, Jean-Luc","Allard, Pierre-Marie","Sichert, Andreas","Pontrelli, Sammy","Pullman, Benjamin S.","Bandeira, Nuno","Gerwick, William H.","Gindro, Katia","Massana-Codina, Josep","Wagner, Berenike C.","Forchhammer, Karl","Petras, Daniel","Aiosa, Nicole","Garg, Neha","Liebeke, Manuel","Bourceau, Patric","Kang, Kyo Bin","Gadhavi, Henna","de Carvalho, Luiz Pedro Sorio","Silva dos Santos, Mariana","Pérez-Lorente, Alicia Isabel","Molina-Santiago, Carlos","Romero, Diego","Franke, Raimo","Brönstrup, Mark","Vera Ponce de León, Arturo","Pope, Phillip Byron","La Rosa, Sabina Leanti","La Barbera, Giorgia","Roager, Henrik M.","Laursen, Martin Frederik","Hammerle, Fabian","Siewert, Bianka","Peintner, Ursula","Licona-Cassani, Cuauhtemoc","Rodriguez-Orduña, Lorena","Rampler, Evelyn","Hildebrand, Felina","Koellensperger, Gunda","Schoeny, Harald","Hohenwallner, Katharina","Panzenboeck, Lisa","Gregor, Rachel","O’Neill, Ellis Charles","Roxborough, Eve Tallulah","Odoi, Jane","Bale, Nicole J.","Ding, Su","Sinninghe Damsté, Jaap S.","Guan, Xue Li","Cui, Jerry J.","Ju, Kou San","Silva, Denise Brentan","Silva, Fernanda Motta Ribeiro","da Silva, Gilvan Ferreira","Koolen, Hector H.F.","Grundmann, Carlismari","Clement, Jason A.","Mohimani, Hosein","Broders, Kirk","McPhail, Kerry L.","Ober-Singleton, Sidnee E.","Rath, Christopher M.","McDonald, Daniel","Knight, Rob","Wang, Mingxun","Dorrestein, Pieter C."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-725045"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dorrestein, Pieter C."],"country":["Austria","Brazil","Costa Rica","Germany","Mexico","Netherlands","Norway","Singapore","South Africa","South Korea","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Agroscope","All Global Affiliations","Bowie State University","Brazilian Agricultural Research Corporation","CSIC - Institute of Subtropical and Mediterranean Horticulture","Carnegie Mellon University","ETH Zürich","Empresa Brasileira de Pesquisa Agropecuária","Georgia Institute of Technology","Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research","Hepatitis B Foundation","Instituto Tecnologico de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey","Kiel University","King's College London","Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine","Massachusetts Institu