 IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Carbon Value and the Salvaging of the Amazon","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381785","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This article offers an anthropological analysis of a Papua New Guinean nationalist ideology deeply inspired by neo- Pentecostalism. The basis for this study comes from ethnographic material collected during my fieldwork in the Parliament of Papua New Guinea (PNG), where I worked with a group of politicians and bureaucrats who have become known for their iconoclastic and evangelical actions, including their (in)famous destruction of traditional carvings. By mapping their narratives of nation building, I examine how two dimensions of Evangelical Christianity, namely, its focus on the Biblical scriptures and its demonology, were central to the formulation of this group's nationalist and postcolonial ideology. This work provides a contribution towards broader discussions on the effect of evangelical movements on nationalism around the contemporary world and, in particular, in the Global South.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Santos da Costa, Priscila"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384907"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Nationalism","Pacific","Papua New Guinea","Post colonialism","neo Pentecostalism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"postcolonialism and neo pentecostalism a case from papua new guinea","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86280947/Postcolonial_Nationalism_article_Santos_da_Costa.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384907","identifier":[{"id":"85102734941","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f6fd38fc-66a6-41dd-9235-9241b672b704"],"keyword":["Pacific","Papua New Guinea","nationalism","neo-Pentecostalism","post-colonialism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8E3B6BA98045B3C5FF06990138F830DF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86280947/Postcolonial_Nationalism_article_Santos_da_Costa.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Priscila","key":"santosdacostapau","last":"Santos da Costa","locid":"9734ef6f-09d1-4ca1-b968-6ad34872d504","name":"Santos da Costa, Priscila","orcid":"0000-0003-2439-9960","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/nana.12731","issn":["13545078","14698129"],"issn_org":["13545078"],"issue":"3","journal":"Nations and Nationalism","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Nations and Nationalism","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102734941"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f6fd38fc-66a6-41dd-9235-9241b672b704"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Postcolonialism and Neo-Pentecostalism : A case from Papua New Guinea","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384907","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
